# Multi-subject — M1a Relation inquiry (explorer ↔ extractor collaboration)
#
# Targets the new HDP multi-subject dispatch + relation hypothesis
# (CritRelationAbsent) introduced in commit b14cfde. Question names
# two agents and asks how they collaborate — a pairwise relation the
# LLM should either mark IsRelationalLookup=true (triggering the
# relation hypothesis) or at minimum produce two anchored hypotheses
# via explainSetHypothesis. Pre-b14cfde behavior: firstSymbol picked
# one of the two and the other was effectively dropped from the
# hypothesis set.
#
# Ground truth (internal/orchestrator/topology.go + explorer.go +
# extractor.go): Explorer runs Turn A (emit_evidence +
# emit_investigation_complete), drops EvidenceItems and
# TurnAArtifacts.ToolResults onto MutableState; Extractor runs Turn B
# (emit_answer_symbol + emit_hypothesis_verdict), reads the Turn A
# output back via BusContext. The collaboration is producer/consumer
# across the two stages, gated by extract being dispatched exactly
# once just before finalize.
#
# EXPECT_SECTIONS enforces symmetry — both agent names must appear.
# EXPECT_CONTAINS pins at least one concrete structural term from
# each side's actual implementation so a vague "they collaborate"
# answer fails.
ID="m1a"
NAME="relation inquiry — explorer and extractor collaboration"
QUESTION="codrax 里的 explorer agent 和 extractor agent 是如何协作的？两者之间的数据是通过什么传递的？分别列出 Turn A 和 Turn B 产出的 emit_* 工具。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="emit_evidence emit_answer_symbol"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py identical same.agent"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="explorer extractor"
